course: dictionary
lesson: 12343
title: A word for anyone who makes things by hand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A craftsperson is someone who makes things skilfully by hand. The word is gender-neutral, so it can be used for a woman or a man. «The craftsperson carved a bowl from a single piece of wood.» The clues are carved and bowl: the person made something with their hands, and they were careful and skilled.
explain: Words are often built from smaller parts. Craft means skill in making things by hand, and person means a human being, so craftsperson is simply a person who has that skill. Craftsman and craftswoman mean the same thing, but each is used for only one gender.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The local craftspeople sold baskets and jewellery at the fair.» If you swap in people who make things skilfully by hand, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A craftsperson is someone who makes things skilfully by hand.
fact: Pots, furniture, jewellery and baskets are all things a craftsperson might make.
fact: «Craftsperson» is gender-neutral, so it is used for a woman or a man.
fact: «A skilled craftsperson» means a person who is very good at making things by hand.
fact: The plural of craftsperson is craftspeople, as in «local craftspeople».
exercise: «The craftsperson wove a basket from willow.» What is a craftsperson? | *Someone who makes things skilfully by hand | Someone who sells food in a shop | Someone who drives a bus | A person who sings in a choir
exercise: Which word is the plural of craftsperson? | crafty | craftsperson's | *craftspeople | craft
exercise: Why do people use craftsperson instead of craftsman or craftswoman? | *It works for any person, whether a woman or a man | It is a kind of tool | It means only men | It means only women
test: «She is a skilled craftsperson who makes silver rings.» What does skilled mean here? | Very noisy | *Very good at something | Very tired | Very far away
test: Which of these would a craftsperson most likely make? | A rainbow | *A clay pot | A thunderstorm | A football match
exam: Which sentence uses craftsperson correctly? | The craftsperson rained all day | The craftsperson ran for the train | *The craftsperson at the fair made a wooden stool by hand | The craftsperson sang a song at the bus stop
